  Capacity line: B at 100K records/day needs about 1,392 calls/min, measured only up to about 399 (10 workers); the rest is extrapolated.
  Highest clean level: 10 workers = 399 calls per minute (no 429 or other error at any level; the SDK retries a 429 twice before it would show). B at 100K records/day needs 1,392 calls per minute, 3.5x that; at the measured near-linear scaling (about 40 calls per minute per worker) that is about 35 workers, UNTESTED above 10. 1M and 10M records/day need 10x and 100x more and would need a higher rate limit from the provider (not measured).

